# A ring between two packages, panel 252's R1 (2026-11-19, the sitting's
# completeness critic's case): `alpha`'s module uses `beta`'s, and `beta`'s
# names `alpha`'s record, each package read from a folder through the
# catalogue beside this file and naming the other in its own. 20 doubled,
# plus one, is 41. A surface fixture rather than a `run` case, since every
# build of a `path` entry says so on stderr. Through fetched entries this
# ring is unrun: an entry fetched by `version` or `git` carries a `sum`
# (`selfhost/module/catalogue.hero`) of every file of its tree, its own
# catalogue among them (`selfhost/module/fingerprint.hero`), so each of two
# such packages would name a fingerprint that covers its own (read, not run).
use <alpha>/a

function main()
    print(a.more(c: a.Count(n: 20)))
